# Code Project Configuration - goldfinger (GRAND SLAM)

Reference copy of the configurable fields for the goldfinger manuscript. The
live file is `config.yaml`. This is a template copy showing the configurable
surface; the canonical values are in `config.yaml`.

paper:
  title: "Goldfinger: GRAND SLAM — Special-Agent Mission Software"
  subtitle: "Gold-Market Cornering, Vault Defense Assessment, and Laser Threat Physics"
  version: "0.1.0"

authors:
  - name: "Daniel Ari Friedman"
    orcid: "0000-0001-6232-9096"
    email: "daniel@activeinference.institute"
    affiliation: "Active Inference Institute"
    corresponding: true

publication:
  journal: "BOND Suite Mission Report"
  year: "2026"

keywords:
  - "gold-market cornering"
  - "supply shock price dynamics"
  - "defense-in-depth security"
  - "vault penetration assessment"
  - "laser threat physics"
  - "burn-through time"

metadata:
  license: "MIT"
  language: "en"

# Deterministic reference intel (mirrored by module REFERENCE_* constants).
grand_slam:
  market:
    reference_price: 1850.0
    supply_0: 100.0
    fraction_removed: 0.30
    elasticity: 1.25
    adjustment: 0.4
    steps: 40
  vault:
    perimeter: 0.70
    fence: 0.60
    guard_response: 0.80
    vault_door: 0.90
    combination_lock: 0.75
    gold_storage: 0.85
  laser:
    power: 5000.0
    area: 1.0e-5
    density: 7800.0
    thickness: 0.05
    specific_heat: 500.0
    delta_temperature: 1500.0
    absorptivity: 0.6
